WEBVTT

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.810
Man, it's so hot.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.440
Abeno-san, I'm amazed you can wear that.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.000
Aren't you hot?

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.020
I am hot.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.030
What? Really?

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.330
Mononokean, come.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:20.290
Am I exaggerating how hot it is?

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:24.270
He seemed exhausted from yesterday's heat.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.480
I'll play with Fuzzy inside 
the Mononokean again today.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.550
It's so cool.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.840
Fuzzy, we're back.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.160
It was hot on the school roof 
since there wasn't any shade.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.500
If you want to play, today we can...

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.440
Huh?

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.900
The ceiling? No, of course not.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.570
Abeno-san, Fuzzy is...

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.200
There's something I want to ask you.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.330
Okay.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.460
Did you steal anything from the Underworld?

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.610
Um...

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.550
I didn't steal anything.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.430
Why did you hesitate?

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.800
Did something come to mind?

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.920
I 100% guarantee I didn't 
steal anything on purpose,

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:26.460
but I thought it might be 
possible I did accidentally.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.060
So you don't remember?

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:30.870
What?

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.650
When you keep asking, it makes me 
lose confidence in my answer...

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.070
You didn't, right? You didn't do it?

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.040
No...

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:41.450
Are you talking about the scroll 
I delivered to the Executive?!

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:45.960
I handed it to his servant 
like I was supposed to!

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.160
Right, Fuzzy?

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.040
Wait, that's right!
 Abeno-san, Fuzzy is missing!

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.520
I know.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:59.470
While you two were gone earlier, 
one of the Justice's servants came...

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.380
Huh?

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:07.100
...and claimed that a servant of the 
Mononokean was suspected of theft...

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.600
...so they arrested him.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.940
Fuzzy's suspected of theft?

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.040
...so they arrested him.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:50.310
<b>Mystery 5 "The Tiger"</b>

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.230
Fuzzy was taken by the Justice for stealing?

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:53.540
They practically kidnapped him before 
I could even ask the servant's name.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:53.540
No...

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:56.590
<i>By theft, could they mean...</i>

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:57.460
Hey.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:03.960
You know what they're 
talking about, don't you?

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.300
Did Fuzzy steal something?

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.490
No, it's not like that!

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:09.930
If we're talking about theft,

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:13.580
there was a thief in the Underworld 
who looked just like Fuzzy.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:14.680
The Fuzzy clone!

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:20.320
Maybe they arrested Fuzzy because 
they mistook him for the Fuzzy clone!

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.290
I'd better go see the Justice.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:24.330
Mononokean.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:29.660
It's odd, though.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.160
Itsuki?

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.540
Abeno-san?

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:39.040
Mononokean, open the door.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.690
Are you going to see the Justice?

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.820
Yeah. Come with me.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.850
Excuse me.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:52.810
Excuse me.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.840
<i>—lo? Hello?</i>

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.300
<i>—lo, Justice?</i>

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.160
<i>You ate one of my tadpoles again, didn't you?</i>

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.200
<i>I thought I forbade you from eating meat.</i>

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.580
Do you need something?

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.340
<i>I'd like to ask about my request.</i>

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.090
About that...

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:27.340
Just like you said, we arrested 
the employee of the Mononokean.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.700
<i>Well done.</i>

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:35.950
This is the employee of the 
Mononokean, Ashiya Hanae.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:39.360
As you requested, we arrested and 
brought him here immediately.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.110
That's not him.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.330
What?

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:47.760
I'm pretty sure I told you he's humanoid.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.360
Transform into your humanoid form!

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.120
You can transform, can't you?

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:54.320
<i>This is the yokai that was with the one</i>

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.920
<i>that helped me find my tail ring 
on the way to the Birdcage.</i>

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:02.410
<i>I assumed he was one of the 
Legislator's employees,</i>

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:04.500
<i>but does this mean he...</i>

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.420
Excuse me, Justice.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:12.080
We were just contacted by a patrol.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.280
The Mononokean is in the Underworld.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:21.150
Hey, was Itsuki— was the master 
accompanied by a humanoid?

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.020
Yes, that's what they reported.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:28.350
You can't transform?

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.780
They must've come to get him back.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.780
Did we arrest the wrong guy?

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:35.280
What is it they say about 
this sort of situation?

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:37.790
Oh, right.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:40.970
"Nothing ventured, 
nothing gained," right?

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:41.930
What?

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:45.800
He's awake!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.470
Abeno-san, Fuzzy clone is awake!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:49.800
Abeno-san!

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.180
Huh? Oh.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.630
Are you all right?

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:57.110
Was it this stuff Koura-san gave us?

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:01.980
If you're going to catch the clone, 
you should give him this sedative.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:04.570
It should work even if he just smells it.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.700
Sure, but it won't be easy to—

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.620
I found the clone!

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:22.180
We captured the hairball clone and 
brought him with us, but most likely...

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:25.460
What?!

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.720
You're that yokai from...

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.120
So you're an employee of the Mononokean, huh?

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:39.380
Abeno-san, this is the 
yokai I met in the forest!

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:42.520
So the Legislator was right.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:48.810
Itsuki, you don't get along with him, do you?

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.460
You can tell?

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.100
Of course. You're an odd couple.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.650
I bet you quarrel a lot.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:56.280
He never shuts up.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.290
He was making a lot of noise earlier, too.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.760
<i>Are they friends who bond over 
insulting people to their faces?</i>

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:05.500
<i>I already figured that Abeno-san 
didn't like me, so I'm fine.</i>

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.110
<i>And being loud is part of my identity!</i>

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:11.630
Oh, right! Abeno-san, this 
is no time for complaining!

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.550
Mr. Justice, please release Fuzzy!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.950
This Fuzzy clone is the real thief 
who's been stealing things!

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.520
It's not Fuzzy. Look closely!

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.020
They're totally different, so please 
acquit Fuzzy of all charges!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.600
You talk crazy fast.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.480
Can you talk even faster?

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:29.850
Do it.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:32.000
That's not what I wanted you to hear!

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.040
I'm telling you...

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.280
That's fine. I'll release Fuzzy.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.280
What? Really?

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.390
Yeah. The Fuzzy clone

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:42.520
will be tried properly here at the 
White Sand Prison, so don't worry.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.380
Take him away.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:46.170
Right.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:51.400
Um... He may have had some 
reason for stealing so much.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.230
Please... be lenient...

00:08:57.350 --> 00:09:02.180
Anyway, as for Fuzzy, I'll 
release him on one condition.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.440
Haven't Fuzzy's charges been cleared?

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.250
I never suspected him in the first place.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:15.070
I was after a human named 
Ashiya this whole time.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.070
Me?

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:20.870
If you remain at the White Sand 
Prison, I'll let Fuzzy go.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.080
That's my condition.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:30.340
Did he suggest that you offer this deal?

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.590
I knew there was something odd about 
the way you were going about this.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:40.350
Even he'd be breaking the law if he 
dragged Ashiya off for no reason.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.600
But so long as you had reason to 
suspect him, you could arrest him.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.350
So...

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:52.750
Did the Executive tell you to bring him here

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:54.220
under suspicion of robbery?

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.190
Huh? The Executive?

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:08.870
Wait a minute. I was the one 
the Justice wanted to arrest,

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.450
but the robbery charges were fake,

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:13.770
and the Executive asked him to do it...

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:16.860
But why would the Executive
want me arrested?

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:21.010
It's not about you specifically.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.660
The Executive hates humans.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.680
Right, Itsuki?

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:29.190
Yeah.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:32.810
<i>A yokai who hates humans?</i>

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.570
A yokai who hates humans?

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:42.460
I guess that's enough. You figured it out.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:46.590
Like you said, Itsuki, the 
Executive asked me to arrest him.

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:48.960
I asked him why,

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.660
but he wouldn't tell me.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:54.810
I don't know anything else.

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:59.420
If you want to know, you only 
need to wait a little longer.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:01.090
The Executive is coming here.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.800
The guy who stays cooped up 
in the Birdcage all year

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.100
is choosing to come here?

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:07.630
Yup. Unusual, isn't it?

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:11.460
When I try to invite him anywhere, 
he always says he's busy and won't come out.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:16.280
I'd better tidy up before 
the Executive gets here.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.860
He transformed, like Yahiko!

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:23.340
You're no fun.

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:25.990
You didn't scream like you did earlier.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:28.440
He criticized my reaction!

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:31.530
Were you not expecting me to come, Itsuki?

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:32.990
Who are you?!

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:36.060
Who do you think I am, Ashiya Hanae?

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.130
The Executive?

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.140
That's correct. Well done.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:46.640
<i>What? What is this?</i>

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.410
<i>I can't speak.</i>

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.200
<i>Am I paralyzed?</i>

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:54.020
<i>I can't even breathe.</i>

00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:58.560
Are you okay?

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.090
I'm fine.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:09.040
Executive, I didn't think you'd come.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.280
I wasn't expecting to, either,

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:15.290
when I heard the Justice had 
failed to arrest Ashiya Hanae.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:18.190
But fortunately, because 
you brought him here,

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:21.210
I didn't waste my time after all.

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:25.300
I didn't tell you we arrested the wrong guy.

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:30.760
I heard the news from the tadpole I keep 
with me through that one right there.

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:33.610
Oh, so the signal didn't drop.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:34.810
You were eavesdropping.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:39.180
You wanted to know why
I sought to have you arrested,

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:41.320
didn't you?

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.570
Very well.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:45.070
I will tell you.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:56.860
Ever since I learned of your existence,

00:12:56.860 --> 00:13:00.250
I've been debating whether 
to let you live or kill you.

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:01.780
<i>Kill me?</i>

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.480
You're a dangerous human

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:09.660
who can see yokai and has entered 
the Underworld where we live.

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.220
Should I kill you,

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:16.420
or allow you to continue living 
as an employee of the Mononokean?

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:21.400
Until I decided, I wanted to keep you 
locked up in the White Sand Prison.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:26.530
<i>Again... I'm paralyzed again...</i>

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:28.960
What's wrong?

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:30.780
Executive, revert to your humanoid form!

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:33.310
How disappointing.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:37.770
I hadn't assumed this form in a while, 
but it doesn't seem too popular.

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:41.210
Still, I shall not transform back yet.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:44.650
Not if he's unable to withstand even this.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:49.140
Can you breathe?

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:52.840
<i>The Executive's aura is too 
strong for Ashiya in this form.</i>

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:54.630
<i>He knew that and transformed anyway.</i>

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.590
Executive, enough is—

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:07.190
Executive...

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:10.320
Revert.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.650
<i>Itsuki laid a hand on the Executive?</i>

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:20.070
<i>He's never done that before.</i>

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:37.310
You struck me, Itsuki.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:38.600
Because you—

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:41.480
Will you protect another human?

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:42.520
What?

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:46.400
When you allowed Egen 
to observe Ashiya Hanae,

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.820
you tried to protect him, didn't you?

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.670
This time you not only protected a human,

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:56.240
but you used violence against a yokai.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:59.750
The true master of the Mononokean,

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:03.110
Aoi, never did anything like that.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.830
Listen to me, Itsuki.

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:10.570
That human, Ashiya Hanae, 
is more dangerous

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:12.970
than you realize.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:17.390
He ought to be killed. 
He's having a negative effect on you.

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:23.400
Well? If you don't want us 
to kill him, will you do it?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.690
Killing an employee is surely possible

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:29.930
for the master of the Mononokean,
since he's above the law.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.030
That's enough!

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.390
Just where do you think we are?

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:38.350
In this place where the guilty 
are judged and made to atone,

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:41.210
you shouldn't be using grievous 
words like "kill," Executive.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:44.460
This is why I didn't say 
anything to you, Justice.

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:48.940
If you knew my reason, you wouldn't 
have listened to my request.

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:53.780
Both of you, come with me.

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:03.500
Ashi—

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:04.490
Itsuki, come.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:09.120
I'll arbitrate your dispute.

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:12.070
It's best if Ashiya-kun's not there.

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:15.000
Wait here.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:20.830
Hey, wait!

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.330
Just because you've been released doesn't 
mean you can do whatever you want!

00:16:28.950 --> 00:16:32.840
Fuzzy... I'm so glad you're okay.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:36.410
<i>I couldn't breathe. I thought 
I was actually going to die.</i>

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:41.600
<i>If Abeno-san hadn't defied the Executive,</i>

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:45.450
<i>I'd be dead right now.</i>

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.360
Executive, you're in the wrong.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:56.860
Article five of the three-branch government 
law forbids personal conflicts.

00:16:56.860 --> 00:17:00.870
It wasn't your place to verbally 
chastise or frighten him like that.

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:04.760
The Legislator is responsible for 
managing the Mononokean's employees.

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:08.140
His management style is too hands-off.

00:17:08.140 --> 00:17:11.880
He never takes anything seriously, so I—

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:13.880
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:18.650
But Itsuki, while he may 
have taken it too far,

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:21.770
I agree with the 
Executive's line of thinking.

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:27.050
The Underworld is the only 
place yokai can live in safety.

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:30.650
If anyone found out about humans 
coming and going freely,

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:34.460
some would be more than a 
little anxious or outraged.

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:39.160
As the Justice, I must ensure that the 
Underworld remains a peaceful place.

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:45.770
So I would prefer that Ashiya Hanae be 
forbidden from entering the Underworld.

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:53.260
Fine.

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:13.690
We're going back to the Mononokean.

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:15.690
Okay.

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:21.070
Ashiya-kun, before you 
leave, we need to talk.

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:22.170
Talk?

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:23.450
Listen...

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:28.650
I'm forbidden from entering the Underworld?

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:34.460
If you can promise you won't enter, 
the Executive says he won't harm you.

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:50.230
I understand.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:53.480
I won't return to the Underworld.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:18:59.490
Ashiya Hanae.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.320
I've heard rather positive things

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:05.600
about the work you've done as 
an employee of the Mononokean.

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:09.750
As long as you're beneficial 
to us, I'll leave you alone.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.650
But should you become a threat,

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:16.750
I will not hesitate to violate 
the law to act against you.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:22.440
Executive, I can't ignore what you just said.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.740
I'm only joking.

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:25.310
Like I told you before,

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:28.220
you're forbidden from approaching 
Ashiya-kun, got it?

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:32.270
I know. I'm walking away from him right now.

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.610
I am returning to the Birdcage.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:39.030
Give my regards to the Legislator.

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:52.040
Fuzzy!

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:59.920
So he was arrested by accident!

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.800
Yeah, apparently so.

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:08.750
Mononokean, take Ashiya home.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:11.060
I'll come back after I visit the Legislator.

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:14.950
I'll have the Legislator reprimand 
the Executive, as well.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:16.560
You should go home and rest.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.700
Okay.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:36.480
<b>Green Tea</b>

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:35.160
<i>He said I have work today, too.</i>

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:39.160
<i>I wonder what kind of yokai 
we'll be exorcising today.</i>

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.220
Hanae?

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:52.560
You startled me! Good morning, Hanae.

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:55.180
Good morning. Your voice is raspy, Mom.

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:57.120
I just woke up. It's not working yet.

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:58.950
<i>I thought she was a yokai!</i>

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:02.600
What's wrong? You're up early today.

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:07.360
Uh... I was hot. I woke up 
because I was thirsty.

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:10.320
Isn't your summer vacation coming up?

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:12.750
I hope you'll help around 
the shop again this year.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:13.900
Sure.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:19.790
What was that for?

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:23.020
Nothing. I just felt like it.

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:27.370
Well, I'm going to get breakfast started.

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:34.200
I'm so glad I'm alive.

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:37.240
Did you enjoy it that much? 
Want me to do it again?

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:39.160
Mom, stop.

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:46.820
<i>What was that power?</i>

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:50.340
<i>Is it something people 
who can see yokai can do?</i>

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:55.040
<i>Does that mean I can, too?</i>

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time: "The Seedling"</b>

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:30.630
I'm joining Ashiya on the photography 
club's overnight trip,

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:33.390
but it could be a good 
opportunity for him to train.

00:23:34.070 --> 00:23:36.390
Next time, "The Seedling."

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:39.110
Yahiko, want to come with us?
